The prime 2: number of solutions modulo 2^k divided by 2^(3k)
  2^1: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: {0: '1'}
  2^2: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: {0: '1/2', 2: '3/2'}
  2^3: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: {0: '1/4', 2: '3/2', 4: '3/4', 6: '3/2'}
  2^4: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: ...
  2^5: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: ...
  2^6: four squares, odd classes: ['1']; det form a1a2+b1b2, odd classes: ['3/4']; four squares even classes: ...
  (four squares: density 1 at every odd class; determinant form: 3/4 = 1 - 1/4 at every odd class)

Jacobi: r_4(n) by direct count against 8 sigma(n) (n odd) and 24 sigma(odd part) (n even), n <= 2000
  r_4(n) = 8 sigma(n) for all odd n <= 2000 and 24 sigma(odd part) for even n: True

Real density: sum_{n <= N} r_4(n) against pi^2 N^2 / 2 (volume of the 4-ball of radius sqrt N)
  N = 500: sum = 1236185 ; pi^2 N^2/2 = 1233700.6; ratio = 1.00201
  N = 1000: sum = 4937225 ; pi^2 N^2/2 = 4934802.2; ratio = 1.00049
  N = 2000: sum = 19739833 ; pi^2 N^2/2 = 19739208.8; ratio = 1.00003

Singular series check: r_4(n) = (pi^2 n) * 1 * prod_{p odd} (1 - p^-2) sigma(p^v)/p^v  = 8 sigma(n) for odd n
  prod_{p odd}(1 - p^-2) = (6/pi^2)/(1 - 1/4) = 8/pi^2 ;  numerically:
  6/pi^2 = 0.6079271019;  (6/pi^2)/(3/4) = 0.8105694691;  8/pi^2 = 0.8105694691
